{%- comment -%}
  zv-woning-floors: prints 0, 1 or 2, the number of extra floors a cart line's `Woning`
  line-item property stands for (spec §7, docs/woning-surcharge-research-2026-09-23.md).

  The two values come from pricing.config.json via zv-pricing (zv_woning_1_value,
  zv_woning_2_value). A legacy value from carts opened before 2026-09-24 starts with
  zv_woning_legacy_prefix ("Groter dan 100 m²", e.g. "Groter dan 100 m² (+€4/mnd per extra
  verdieping of per 100 m² extra woonoppervlak)") and counts as 1 floor. Anything else,
  including blank, is 0.

  Params (render scope can't see the section's zv_* variables, so pass them in):
    value  - the property value, e.g. item.properties['Woning']
    v1, v2 - zv_woning_1_value, zv_woning_2_value
    legacy - zv_woning_legacy_prefix
  Usage: capture it, then `| strip | plus: 0` to get a number.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign n = 0
  if value != blank
    if value == v2
      assign n = 2
    elsif value == v1
      assign n = 1
    elsif legacy != blank
      assign legacy_len = legacy | size
      assign head = value | slice: 0, legacy_len
      if head == legacy
        assign n = 1
      endif
    endif
  endif
  echo n
-%}
